From b20720d6fbd703d46cda8e542935ee1cdfd99c16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guy Lyons <guylyons2@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 23:58:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] macos-arm64: sun shadows from dynamic objects, on by
 default

The sun direction now follows vrad's construction (SetupLightNormalFromProps,
negated); the previous AngleVectors form was mirrored in the horizontal plane.
Shadow rays only darken where a dynamic object blocks a point the world brushes
leave sunlit, so the lightmaps' own shadows are not doubled. Static props are a
separate instance so tree branches and rooftop props (which vrad did not shadow
with) do not count as baked shadow. Instance masks proved unreliable on the M1
software tracer, so hits are walked and classified by instance id instead. A
per-object bounds pre-test keeps the shadow ray cost to the objects' footprints.
rt_dump_world writes the traced world triangles for offline checks.
